<section class="demo">
  <div class="wrap">
    <h2 class="h2">One method. Watch what it changes.</h2>
    <p class="sub">A real example from Chapter 5: a roastery owner chasing a late shipment. The same six-part brief drives research, data analysis, and build prompts later in the book.</p>
    <div class="demo-grid" id="cwg-demo">
      <div class="panel weak">
        <p class="ptag">What most people type</p>
        <p class="prompt" data-type>Write an email to the supplier about the late shipment.</p>
        <div class="mail">Subject: Shipment Delay

Dear <mark>[Supplier Name]</mark>,

I hope this email finds you well. I am writing to inquire about the status of our recent order, which appears to have been delayed. <mark>We apologize for any inconvenience this inquiry may cause.</mark>

We would greatly appreciate it if you could provide an update <mark>at your earliest convenience</mark>.

Best regards, <mark>[Your Name]</mark></div>
        <p class="verdict">Blanks to fill, an apology you didn't want, and no deadline anyone has to meet.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="panel strong">
        <p class="ptag">The ARROWS brief you'll learn to write</p>
        <div class="prompt arrows" data-lines>
          <div><i>A</i><span><em>Aim:</em> a confirmed ship date within 48 hours, relationship intact.</span></div>
          <div><i>R</i><span><em>Reality:</em> I own Nada Roastery in Amman; Finca Verde has supplied us for 3 years.</span></div>
          <div><i>R</i><span><em>Request:</em> an email about PO-2291, 120 kg due 1 September, 3 weeks late, 10 days of stock left.</span></div>
          <div><i>O</i><span><em>Output:</em> English, 100 to 150 words, clear subject line.</span></div>
          <div><i>W</i><span><em>Walls:</em> firm and friendly. No apologizing, threats, or flattery.</span></div>
          <div><i>S</i><span><em>Standard:</em> end with two requests they can answer.</span></div>
        </div>
        <div class="mail">Subject: <span class="ok">PO-2291 — confirmed ship date needed within 48 hours</span>

Dear Finca Verde team,

Our order PO-2291 (120 kg of green Huila) was due on 1 September. Three weeks later it has not shipped, and our last two emails have gone unanswered. Our stock covers only ten more days, so within 48 hours we need:

<span class="ok">1. A confirmed shipping date.</span>
<span class="ok">2. The tracking number as soon as it is issued.</span>

Rana, Nada Roastery, Amman</div>
